  { A wait on the poller is armed with a token, not with the routine: the
    record in the low 48 bits, a number of 16 bits in the top ones, and
    G+192 holds that number + 1 while the routine waits (G+200 the last
    number). Whoever wakes it first takes G+192 back to 0 with a CAS, so
    an event left over from an earlier wait finds another number and is
    dropped: a routine that had read a descriptor and gone on to wait on
    a channel was woken by that descriptor again and took it for the
    channel's wake (1.0.57). A registration is one-shot, so a ready
    descriptor raises one event per wait instead of one per poll.
