  { CanSpin, Nanotime and the first-come queue of the mutex (P98).
    rt_canspin is Go's sync_runtime_canSpin: spinning pays only while
    other Ps run (nproc > idle + spinning + 1) and this P has nothing
    else to run, neither runnext nor its local queue. rt_qwaitback and
    rt_qwaitfront queue the current routine at the end or the front of
    a two-word queue (first, last; the link is G+232); rt_qwakefirst
    takes the first one, or 0. Nanotime is rt_now. }
  Line('rt_canspin:');
